---
id: org.dxos.plugin.terra
name: TerraPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

A deterministic 3D planet plugin for `DXOS` Composer, rendering seed-driven stylized worlds
with `Babylon.js`. A single seed always produces the same land, water, and biome layout, so
planets are fully reproducible and shareable by seed alone.

Terrain is generated procedurally — elevation and biome placement derive from layered simplex
noise seeded via `seedrandom` — and rendered as a stylized low-poly sphere with distinct land,
water, and biome coloring.

Live parameters (seed, noise scale, sea level, biome thresholds) let users reshape the planet
in real-time without leaving Composer; this scaffold will be filled in with the engine,
components, and ECHO-backed types in subsequent tasks.
